| **Pending** | 27 TEAM_MEMBERS eeNum records left blank — awaiting Workday pull | Internal |
| **Future** | Auth upgrade: SHA-256 passphrase → Okta/SharePoint SSO before broader rollout | — |
| **Future** | TEAM_MEMBERS live feed integration — when Workday (or equivalent HR system) is connected, employee status should gate inclusion in the TEAM_MEMBERS feed at the source. Employees who are offboarded or transitioned out of ES will stop appearing automatically. No parallel removal mechanism should be built in the Command Center — the data source is the single source of truth. The identity system (IDENTITY_FROM_TM) is already built to reconstruct at runtime from TEAM_MEMBERS, so the switch to a live feed requires no architectural changes. | Internal |
| **Future** | TEAM_MEMBERS overlap window — between when an employee is closed out in the Command Center (Offboarding or Transitions complete) and when HR removes them from the active employee feed, a brief overlap exists where they may still appear in identity/HM dropdowns. This is acceptable and low-risk; it resolves automatically once the live feed is connected. No action required. | — |


# **13.  Global Design Rules — Non-Negotiable**

| **Rule** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| **No strikethrough — ever** | Completed tasks, done states, and checked items are NEVER shown with strikethrough text (text-decoration:line-through). Done states are indicated by muted color (var(--muted)) and a filled green checkbox only. This applies to every workspace, every task list, every process step, site-wide, without exception. |

